<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέξ-ειμι</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶμι</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ibo</i>) serving as 
				Att.
			
			fut. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεξέρχομαι,</span> to
			which it also supplies the impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῄειν,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήϊσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.223
				</span></i>
			:—<i>go out against</i> an enemy, l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.21
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τισί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.97
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς πολεμίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
					7.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ ἐς μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.23
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>get out, escape,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				937a28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>proceed against, take vengeance on,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.143
			</span></i>; esp. in legal sense, <i>prosecute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.216
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				140
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ φόνου</span>
			<i>for</i> murder, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				866b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				4e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὶ ὑπὲρ φόνου</span>
			ib.b, cf. e: c. acc. pers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεξῇμεν τοῦ
				φόνου τὸν Ἀρίσταρχον</span> Test. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.107
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.11
			</span></i>, etc.: c. dat. rei, <i>visit, avenge,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ παθήματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					866b
				</span></i>
			 (and c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν τῶν πατέρων θάνατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					4.66
				</span></i>
			); also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. δίκῃ, γραφῇ,</span>
			<i>prosecute</i> at law, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				754e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				4c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.93
			</span></i>; <i>attack,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ λόγῳ μεγαλοπρεπέστερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					215e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>go over, traverse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Clearch.
					37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in writing,
				<i>traverse, go through in detail,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμικρὰ καὶ μεγάλα ἄστεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1118
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσας τὰς ἀμφισβητήσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					437a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>go through with, execute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρασκευὰς λόγῳ καλῶς μεμφόμενοι
					ἀνομοίως ἔργῳ ἐπεξιέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τὰς τιμωρίας ἔτι μείζους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.82
				</span></i>
			.</div>
